@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Income Tax Ordinance [New Version] and the Income Tax (Rules for
-- Rounding Amounts) Order 5746-1986: special rates and other regimes (row IL-30).
-- THE NOUNS: DECLARE and nothing else. Every rules module imports this one.
--
-- Sources, all deposited, none fetched by this row (hashes in encoding.json):
--   the Ordinance   ../../registers/source-bundle/income-tax-ordinance-new-version.he.wiki.txt
--   the Order       ../../registers/source-bundle/regulations/income-tax-rules-for-rounding-amounts-order-5746-1986.he.wiki.txt
--   the RE Tax Law  ../../../real-estate-taxation-law-5723-1963/registers/source-bundle/real-estate-taxation-law-5723-1963.he.wiki.txt
-- Hebrew Wikisource raw MediaWiki: unofficial consolidations. A `src:N` comment quotes line N of
-- the one source file its module names, copied mechanically; nothing in Hebrew here is typed by hand.
--
-- Money is new Israeli shekels (NIS), as a bare NUMBER. Rates are percent literals as printed.
-- Membership test for this module: a witness of ordinary competence could testify to the fact,
-- or a return or register records it. Whether the fact makes tax payable is a rule, and belongs
-- in the module of the section that says so.

§ `Nouns for the special rates and other regimes (row IL-30)`

§§ `Section 88 — who holds what, and the facts of a sale`

-- Section 88 defines "means of control" in a body of persons by five rights. A person's holding is the
-- fraction (a percent literal such as 10%) he holds of each kind, directly or indirectly. Whether he
-- holds indirectly through another body is a computation outside this row, so each fraction is an input.
-- The five kinds, in the order of paragraphs (1) to (5) of the definition (source lines 3250-3254):
DECLARE `Holdings of means of control in one body of persons` HAS
    `fraction of the right to profits`                                              IS A NUMBER  -- (1)
    `fraction of the right to appoint a director or general manager`                IS A NUMBER  -- (2)
    `fraction of the voting rights in the general meeting`                          IS A NUMBER  -- (3)
    `fraction of the right to a share of the surplus assets on winding up`          IS A NUMBER  -- (4)
    `fraction of the right to direct the holder of a right in (1) to (4) on how to use it` IS A NUMBER  -- (5)

-- "Relative", s 88: four paragraphs (source lines 3296-3301). The tie of one person to the person asked about.
DECLARE `A family tie of paragraph (1) of the definition of "relative"` IS ONE OF
    `spouse`
    `sibling`
    `parent`
    `parent of a parent`
    `descendant`
    `descendant of a spouse`
    `the spouse of a spouse, sibling, parent, parent of a parent, descendant, or descendant of a spouse`

DECLARE `A family tie of paragraph (2) of the definition of "relative"` IS ONE OF
    `descendant of a sibling`
    `sibling of a parent`

-- Paragraph (3): a body of persons in the holding of a person or his relative, a person holding it, and a
-- body held by a person holding it. "Holding" there is 25% or more of at least one kind of means of control.
-- Paragraph (4): a trustee as defined in s 75C, as to the settlor of a trust of Israeli residents or of a trust
-- of the kind the paragraph names, and as to the beneficiary of a trust whose beneficiary is a non-resident
-- or of a trust under a will. Whether a trustee stands in that tie is a fact the caller supplies.
DECLARE `A tie between two persons, for the definition of "relative"` IS ONE OF
    `a tie of paragraph (1)`  HAS `which tie of paragraph (1)` IS A `A family tie of paragraph (1) of the definition of "relative"`
    `a tie of paragraph (2)`  HAS `which tie of paragraph (2)` IS A `A family tie of paragraph (2) of the definition of "relative"`
    `a body of persons held by the person or by a relative of the person` HAS `largest fraction held of any kind of means of control` IS A NUMBER
    `a person who holds the person`                                        HAS `largest fraction held of any kind of means of control` IS A NUMBER
    `a body of persons held by one who holds the person`                   HAS `largest fraction held of any kind of means of control` IS A NUMBER
    `a trustee as paragraph (4) describes`
    `no tie`

-- A person who might hold "together with" the person asked about.
DECLARE `A person who may hold together with the person` HAS
    `holdings`                                                                 IS A `Holdings of means of control in one body of persons`
    `tie to the person`                                                        IS A `A tie between two persons, for the definition of "relative"`
    `regularly cooperates with the person by agreement on material matters of the body` IS A BOOLEAN

-- "At the time of sale, or at any time in the 12 months before it": the holdings of the person on each day recorded.
DECLARE `The holdings of a person on one day` HAS
    `the day`                                      IS A DATE
    `the person's own holdings that day`           IS A `Holdings of means of control in one body of persons`
    `the others who may hold together with the person that day` IS A LIST OF `A person who may hold together with the person`

-- Fork S1. "Alone or together with another" in "material shareholder": one other person
-- or any number of them. Three relatives holding 4% each give 12% with two others and at most 8% with one.
DECLARE `A reading of "together with another"` IS ONE OF
    `together with any number of others, their holdings added`
    `together with one other person only`
    `declined where the number of others changes the answer`   -- the default

-- Fork S2. S 88 "real capital gain until the fixed date" is the real gain times the ratio of two periods, "from the
-- purchase day to the day before the fixed date" over "from the purchase day to the sale day". The text does not say
-- how the days of a period "from A to B" are counted.
DECLARE `A reading of how the days of a period are counted` IS ONE OF
    `both the first and the last day are counted`
    `the days between the first day and the last day, the first not counted`
    `declined where the way of counting changes the answer`    -- the default

-- Fork S3. "Adjusted remaining original price" leaves out the remaining improvement expenses and half of the remaining
-- holding expenses from the part indexed from the purchase day, and adds back the improvement expenses only.
DECLARE `A reading of half the holding expenses in the adjusted price` IS ONE OF
    `the half of the holding expenses that is left out is lost from the adjusted price`
    `the half of the holding expenses that is left out is added back, not indexed`
    `declined where half the holding expenses changes the answer`   -- the default

-- How an asset came to the taxpayer, for "original price" (six cases, three of them with sub-cases) and for "purchase day".
DECLARE `How the asset came to the taxpayer` IS ONE OF
    `bought`                                                                HAS `the amount the taxpayer spent buying it` IS A NUMBER
    `received in exchange`                                                  HAS `the consideration at the time of the exchange` IS A NUMBER
    `received as a gift before 3 December 1951`                             HAS `the value of the asset when the taxpayer received it` IS A NUMBER
    `received as a gift from 3 December 1951 to 31 March 1968`              HAS `the remaining original price when the last acquirer other than by gift gave it` IS A NUMBER
    `received as a gift from 1 April 1968, not from a relative`             HAS `the consideration on the sale day` IS A NUMBER
    `received as a gift from 1 April 1968 that is exempt under section 97(a)(4) or (5)` HAS `the remaining original price when the last acquirer other than by an exempt gift gave it` IS A NUMBER
    `received as a gift from 1 April 1968 from a relative, not exempt`      HAS `the consideration on the sale day` IS A NUMBER
    `inherited`                                                             HAS `the value of the asset on the day the decedent died` IS A NUMBER
    `created by the taxpayer`                                               HAS `the amount the taxpayer spent creating it` IS A NUMBER
    `arrived in some other way`                                             HAS `the amount the taxpayer spent acquiring it` IS A NUMBER

-- One improvement of the asset: the remaining expense on it and the index on the day it was finished.
DECLARE `An improvement of the asset` HAS
    `remaining expense of the improvement` IS A NUMBER
    `index on the day the improvement was finished` IS A NUMBER

-- A sale of an asset: the figures section 88 computes from.
-- * `consideration`: already net of the expenses of the sale (the s 88 definition of consideration deducts them).
-- * `remaining original price`: the original price, with the improvement and holding expenses not deducted before,
--   less depreciation (the s 88 definition of the remaining original price).
-- * the improvements are listed apart because they are indexed from the day they were finished.
-- * `remaining holding expenses`: part of the remaining original price.
-- The three index readings are the consumer price index as last published before the day (the s 88 definition of the index).
DECLARE `A sale of an asset` HAS
    `consideration`                                                      IS A NUMBER
    `remaining original price`                                           IS A NUMBER
    `improvements`                                                       IS A LIST OF `An improvement of the asset`
    `remaining holding expenses`                                         IS A NUMBER
    `index on the sale day`                                              IS A NUMBER
    `index on the purchase day`                                          IS A NUMBER
    `index on 31 December 1993`                                          IS A NUMBER
    `purchase day`                                                       IS A DATE
    `sale day`                                                           IS A DATE

-- Fork S4. "Material shareholder ... at the time of sale or at any time in the 12 months before it": from which day the
-- twelve months run. For a sale on 15 March 2026: from 15 March 2025, or from 16 March 2025.
DECLARE `A reading of the twelve months before a day` IS ONE OF
    `the twelve months begin on the day twelve months before`
    `the twelve months begin on the day after the day twelve months before`
    `declined where the first day of the twelve months changes the answer`    -- the default

-- Fork V1. Section 91(f)(1) adds "1% for each year from tax year 1949 until the year of acquisition".
DECLARE `A reading of the years counted from 1949 in section 91(f)(1)` IS ONE OF
    `1949 and the year of acquisition are both counted`
    `1949 is counted and the year of acquisition is not`
    `declined where the number of years changes the answer`                  -- the default

-- Fork V2. Section 91(f)(2): "from tax year 2005, 1% is added for each tax year or part of one".
DECLARE `A reading of the years counted from 2005 in section 91(f)(2)` IS ONE OF
    `2005 and the tax year of the sale are both counted`
    `2005 is not counted: the years after it up to the tax year of the sale`
    `declined where the number of years changes the answer`                  -- the default

-- Fork T1. "A rate not exceeding 25%" and "regard the gain as the highest layer of the taxable income" (s 91(b)(1), (b1)(2); s 125C(b)):
-- the section does not say how a cap applies when the gain stands in more than one band of the scale of s 121, some below the cap
-- and some above it.
DECLARE `A reading of a cap on the rate where the gain stands in several bands` IS ONE OF
    `the rate of each band is capped`            -- each shekel is taxed at the lesser of its band's rate and the cap
    `the average rate over the whole gain is capped`   -- the tax is the lesser of the tax at the bands' rates and the cap times the gain
    `declined where the way of applying the cap changes the answer`   -- the default

-- Fork T2. Section 91(b1)(1) taxes three parts of one real gain at different rates, and (b1)(2) regards "the gain" as the highest layer of
-- the taxable income. It does not say where each part stands within that layer, and the bands of the scale differ in rate.
DECLARE `A reading of where each part of a gain stands in the top layer` IS ONE OF
    `each part stands alone on top of the other income`
    `the parts stand one above another, the earliest period lowest`
    `the parts stand one above another, the earliest period highest`
    `declined where the order of the parts changes the answer`        -- the default

-- A band of the marginal scale of section 121: the top of the band (NOTHING for the last band, which has none) and its rate.
-- The caller lists the bands from the lowest, as section 121 prints them for the individual.
DECLARE `A band of a marginal scale` HAS
    `upper limit of the band` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `rate of the band`        IS A NUMBER

-- Fork D1. Section 125B(3): a family company's dividend is taxed at 30% "if the assessee, as meant in s 64A, was a material
-- shareholder, directly or indirectly, in the company that paid". Paragraphs (2) and (5) say "at the time of receiving the dividend or
-- at some time in the twelve months before it"; paragraph (3) says only "was", and names no time.
DECLARE `A reading of the time at which section 125B(3) tests the shareholding` IS ONE OF
    `at the time of receiving the dividend only`
    `at the time of receiving the dividend or at some time in the twelve months before it`
    `declined where the time of the test changes the answer`    -- the default

-- Fork D2. Section 91(b)(3): "20% for a material shareholder". Paragraph (2) names the time (at the sale or at some time in the twelve
-- months before it); paragraph (3) names none.
DECLARE `A reading of the time at which section 91(b)(3) tests the shareholding` IS ONE OF
    `at the time of the sale only`
    `at the time of the sale or at some time in the twelve months before it`
    `declined where the time of the sale test changes the answer`            -- the default

-- Fork V3. Section 91(b1)(1A): for a security bought before the fixed date, "for computing the real capital gain up to the fixed date and the
-- remainder of the real capital gain" the real gain is regarded as reduced by the distributable profits of s 94B. It does not say whether the
-- real gain from the fixed date to the change date, the middle part, is the reduced one too.
DECLARE `A reading of the real gain used for the middle part of a security bought before the fixed date` IS ONE OF
    `the gain reduced by the distributable profits is used for all three parts`
    `the gain before the reduction is used for the middle part`
    `declined where the real gain used for the middle part changes the answer`   -- the default

-- Fork L1. The Real Estate Taxation Law (s 47) defines its "tax year" as twelve months beginning on 1 April, and its s 48A(d) counts by "tax year 1948",
-- "1949 to 1960", "2005", "2011", "2012", "2013 onward". It does not say whether a year beginning on 1 April 2012 is "tax year 2012" or "tax year 2013".
DECLARE `A reading of how a tax year of the Real Estate Taxation Law is named` IS ONE OF
    `named by the calendar year in which it begins`
    `named by the calendar year in which it ends`
    `declined where the naming of the tax year changes the answer`        -- the default

-- The readings of every fork of this row's sections 88, 91, 125B and 125C, as one argument.
DECLARE `The readings of the forks in sections 88, 91, 125B and 125C` HAS
    `together with another`                  IS A `A reading of "together with another"`
    `counting the days of a period`          IS A `A reading of how the days of a period are counted`
    `half the holding expenses`              IS A `A reading of half the holding expenses in the adjusted price`
    `the twelve months before a day`         IS A `A reading of the twelve months before a day`
    `the years from 1949 in section 91(f)(1)` IS A `A reading of the years counted from 1949 in section 91(f)(1)`
    `the years from 2005 in section 91(f)(2)` IS A `A reading of the years counted from 2005 in section 91(f)(2)`
    `a cap where the gain stands in several bands` IS A `A reading of a cap on the rate where the gain stands in several bands`
    `where each part stands in the top layer` IS A `A reading of where each part of a gain stands in the top layer`
    `the time of the test in section 125B(3)` IS A `A reading of the time at which section 125B(3) tests the shareholding`
    `the time of the test in section 91(b)(3)` IS A `A reading of the time at which section 91(b)(3) tests the shareholding`
    `the real gain for the middle part` IS A `A reading of the real gain used for the middle part of a security bought before the fixed date`
    `the naming of a tax year of the Real Estate Taxation Law` IS A `A reading of how a tax year of the Real Estate Taxation Law is named`

§§ `Section 125B — who receives the dividend`

-- The recipient of a dividend, in the five kinds paragraphs (1) to (5) of s 125B name, and any other.
-- * the records are the recipient's holdings in the body that paid the dividend, one record per day on which the holdings are known;
--   a day with no record is a day on which nothing is known (the caller records every day the holdings changed).
-- * for a family company, paragraph (3) tests "the assessee as meant in s 64A", the person who stands behind it, so the records are his.
DECLARE `The recipient of a dividend, for section 125B` IS ONE OF
    `an individual`                                                         HAS `the individual's holdings in the paying body` IS A LIST OF `The holdings of a person on one day`
    `a family company`                                                      HAS `the holdings in the paying company of the person meant in section 64A` IS A LIST OF `The holdings of a person on one day`
    `a public institution or a provident fund as defined in section 9(2)`   HAS `the dividend is exempt from tax in its hands` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a non-resident body of persons`                                        HAS `the body's holdings in the paying body` IS A LIST OF `The holdings of a person on one day`
    `any other recipient`

§§ `Section 125C — interest received by an individual`

-- Section 125C(c)(1): the property on which the interest is paid "is not linked to the index, or is linked in part to the rate of rise
-- of the index, in whole or in part, or is not linked to the index until redemption or repayment".
DECLARE `How the property carrying the interest is linked to the index` IS ONE OF
    `fully linked to the index`
    `linked to the index in part of the rate of rise`
    `not linked to the index`
    `not linked to the index until redemption or repayment`

-- The facts of one receipt of interest by an individual that s 125C(b) to (e) turn on. Each condition of (d) is a fact the caller records.
DECLARE `Interest received by an individual, for section 125C` HAS
    `the interest`                                                                 IS A NUMBER
    `how the property carrying the interest is linked`                             IS A `How the property carrying the interest is linked to the index`
    `the interest is income under section 2(1), or is recorded or must be recorded in the individual's books` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (d)(1)
    `the individual claimed a deduction of interest expenses and linkage differences on the property`          IS A BOOLEAN   -- (d)(2)
    `the individual's holdings in the paying body`                                 IS A LIST OF `The holdings of a person on one day`  -- (d)(3)
    `the individual is an employee of the paying body, supplies it services, sells it goods, or has other special relations with it` IS A BOOLEAN  -- (d)(4)
    `the individual proved to the assessing officer that the rate of interest was fixed in good faith and not influenced by those relations` IS A BOOLEAN -- (d)(4)
    `paid from a study fund before the periods of section 9(16A) or (16B) passed, or from a provident fund for benefits to which section 3(d) applies` IS A BOOLEAN -- (d)(5)
    `another condition set by the Minister of Finance with the approval of the Finance Committee holds`         IS A BOOLEAN   -- (d)(6)
    `paid from a provident fund that is neither a fund for benefits nor a study fund, or from a fund for benefits taxed under section 87`  IS A BOOLEAN   -- (e), first limb
    `the interest is treated as interest income under section 3(h4)(3)`            IS A BOOLEAN   -- (e), the exception

-- What section 125C makes of the interest.
-- * `taxed at the rates of section 121 with the rest of the income`: (d) puts the interest on the scale of s 121 with the rest of the
--   income. The tax then depends on where the interest stands among the other income, which (d) does not say, so no figure is given
--   here: the tax is that of section 121 on the total (row IL-03).
-- * `taxed apart, the tax being`: (b) or (c) gives the tax.
-- * `outside section 125C`: (e) takes the payment out of the section.
DECLARE `What section 125C makes of the interest` IS ONE OF
    `taxed at the rates of section 121 with the rest of the income`
    `taxed apart, the tax being` HAS `the tax` IS A NUMBER
    `outside section 125C`

§§ `Section 122 — the rental of a residential apartment`

-- One payment that may be "qualifying rent" under s 122(f)(1): rent for an apartment in Israel the payer rented to live in, or the annual
-- payment for keeping the payer or the payer's cohabiting spouse in an old people's home (RE Tax Law s 49YG) or a geriatric hospital
-- (s 29C of the Public Health Ordinance 1940), in the tax year, not paid to a relative of paragraph (1) or (2) of the definition in s 88.
DECLARE `A payment of rent or of care fees` HAS
    `the amount`                                                                          IS A NUMBER
    `rent for an apartment in Israel the payer rented to live in`                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `the annual payment for keeping the payer or the payer's cohabiting spouse in an old people's home or a geriatric hospital` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person paid`                                                                     IS A `A tie between two persons, for the definition of "relative"`
    `the payer is the individual, their cohabiting spouse, or a child under 18 living with them` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the payment, or part of it, was claimed in computing the taxable income of the individual or of another` IS A BOOLEAN

-- The facts of one year of letting a residential apartment in Israel by an individual (with their cohabiting spouse and children under 18
-- treated as one owner, s 122(f)(3)).
DECLARE `The letting of a residential apartment, for section 122` HAS
    `the apartment is used for living and is in Israel`                                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `the rental income is income from a business under section 2(1)`                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `the rental income of the individual, their cohabiting spouse and children under 18`   IS A NUMBER
    `the apartment is the only apartment of the individual, within the meaning of section 9(c1c)(4) of the Real Estate Taxation Law` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the payments of rent and care fees in the year`                                       IS A LIST OF `A payment of rent or of care fees`
    `the maximum depreciation or other write-down that could have been deducted for the years of the election, but for section 122(c)` IS A NUMBER

§§ `Section 91 — the seller, what was sold, and the sale`

-- The seller: an individual (b), with the holdings in the body whose security is sold or that issued the bond, for the material shareholder
-- tests of (b)(2) and (b)(3); or a body of persons (a), taxed at the rate of s 126(a), an input here (s 126 is not encoded by this row).
DECLARE `The seller, for section 91` IS ONE OF
    `an individual`      HAS `the individual's holdings in the body whose security is sold, or that issued the bond` IS A LIST OF `The holdings of a person on one day`
    `a body of persons`  HAS `the rate of tax on a body of persons under section 126(a)` IS A NUMBER

-- The kinds of asset s 91 distinguishes.
DECLARE `The kind of asset sold, for section 91` IS ONE OF
    `a security in a body of persons`
    `a bond, commercial security, loan note or loan that is not linked to the index`   -- (b)(3); "not linked" is defined in (b)(3)(c)
    `goodwill that was not paid for`                                                    -- outside (b1)
    `any other asset`

-- A sale of an asset, with the figures s 88 computes (the real capital gain, the capital gain, the chargeable inflationary amount), which
-- ito-88-definitions.l4 computes from a sale record and which a caller may take from it or from the assessment.
DECLARE `A sale for section 91` HAS
    `the seller`                                                         IS A `The seller, for section 91`
    `the kind of asset sold`                                             IS A `The kind of asset sold, for section 91`
    `registered for trading on a stock exchange`                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `registered for trading on a stock exchange before the change date`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `a unit in an exempt mutual fund`                                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `the real capital gain`                                              IS A NUMBER
    `the capital gain`                                                   IS A NUMBER
    `the chargeable inflationary amount`                                 IS A NUMBER
    `the purchase day`                                                   IS A DATE
    `the sale day`                                                       IS A DATE
    `the asset is a security`                                            IS A BOOLEAN
    `the distributable profits of section 94B deducted for a security bought before the fixed date` IS A NUMBER
    `the asset was expropriated`                                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `the tax year in which the asset reached the seller`                 IS A NUMBER
    `the part of the real gain equal to depletion, exploration and development deductions or film production expenses on a unit in an oil or film partnership` IS A NUMBER

-- One tax year of the period over which a gain is spread under s 91(e): the other taxable income of that year, the scale of s 121 for it,
-- and the value of the credit points not used against that income.
DECLARE `A tax year in the period of spreading` HAS
    `the other taxable income that year`                  IS A NUMBER
    `the scale of section 121 for that year`              IS A LIST OF `A band of a marginal scale`
    `the value of the credit points left unused that year` IS A NUMBER

§§ `Section 8(c) — income spread over several tax years`

-- One share of an amount, placed in a tax year.
DECLARE `A share of an amount placed in one tax year` HAS
    `the tax year` IS A NUMBER
    `the amount`   IS A NUMBER

-- A wage difference or an annuity difference, with the tax year it relates to (s 8(c)(1)).
DECLARE `A difference of wages or of an annuity` HAS
    `the tax year the difference relates to` IS A NUMBER
    `the amount of the difference`           IS A NUMBER

-- The income s 8(c) lets the taxpayer or the heirs ask to have placed in other years, with the facts each paragraph turns on.
DECLARE `Income to be spread under section 8(c)` IS ONE OF
    `wage differences or annuity differences`
        HAS `the differences` IS A LIST OF `A difference of wages or of an annuity`                          -- (1)
    `vacation redemption pay received by an employee`
        HAS `the amount of the vacation pay`              IS A NUMBER                                         -- (2)
            `the number of tax years the requester chose` IS A NUMBER
            `the number of years of the employee's work`  IS A NUMBER
    `a grant or a commutation of an annuity of paragraph (5) or (6) of the definition of income from personal exertion`
        HAS `the amount of the grant or commutation`      IS A NUMBER                                         -- (3)
            `the working years the grant is paid for, or the years in which the annuity right arose` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
            `the years the Director allowed instead`      IS A MAYBE (LIST OF NUMBER)

-- Fork E1. (1): differences are placed "in the years to which they relate, but no more than six tax years ending in the year in which they were
-- received". A difference that relates to an earlier year than the six is not placed by the text.
DECLARE `A reading of differences that relate to years before the six tax years` IS ONE OF
    `an older difference is placed in the year of receipt`
    `an older difference is placed in the earliest of the six tax years`
    `declined where the place of an older difference changes the answer`      -- the default

-- Fork E2. (3): equal annual parts "in the working years for which the grant is paid ... but no more than the six tax years ending in the year
-- of receipt". Where the working years end before the year of receipt the six years and the working years part company.
DECLARE `A reading of working years outside the six tax years` IS ONE OF
    `only the working years inside the six tax years count`
    `the last six working years count, wherever they fall`
    `declined where the working years outside the six tax years change the answer`    -- the default

§§ `Section 64A1 — the transparent company`

-- The facts that make a company a transparent company (s 64A1(a), the definition of "חברה שקופה", paragraphs (1) to (8)).
DECLARE `A company that may be transparent` HAS
    `the company is resident in Israel`                                                                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the company is a public company as defined in section 1 of the Companies Law, or its articles allow it to become one` IS A BOOLEAN  -- (1)
    `the number of shareholders, counting spouses and their children, heirs of a shareholder, and buyers from a shareholder in an involuntary sale, as one` IS A NUMBER  -- (2)
    `the Director approved a higher number of shareholders, up to`                                                       IS A MAYBE NUMBER  -- (2)
    `every shareholder is an individual resident in Israel`                                                              IS A BOOLEAN  -- (3)
    `the shares are all of one type except for voting rights, and the shareholders cannot change the rights the shares carry except voting rights` IS A BOOLEAN  -- (4)
    `the right to the company's profits comes from the shares alone`                                                     IS A BOOLEAN  -- (5)
    `each shareholder's right to profits is the same as his right to the company's assets on winding up`                IS A BOOLEAN  -- (6)
    `the company is a financial institution as defined in the Value Added Tax Law`                                       IS A BOOLEAN  -- (7)
    `the company asked to be a transparent company by a notice signed by all its shareholders and delivered to the assessing officer within 60 days of its incorporation` IS A BOOLEAN  -- (8)
    `regulations under section 64A1 are in force`                                                                        IS A BOOLEAN

-- A shareholder of a transparent company, with the figures the attribution of (b) needs.
DECLARE `A shareholder of a transparent company` HAS
    `the fraction of the right to profits`                      IS A NUMBER
    `the company's income of the year that is exempt from tax`  IS A NUMBER

§§ `Section 64A2 — definitions for the real-estate investment fund`

-- The facts about a parcel of land that decide whether it is "yielding land" (מקרקעין מניבים), s 64A2(a).
DECLARE `A parcel of land held by a real-estate investment fund` HAS
    `income under section 2(1) or 2(6) arises from letting it and from activity ancillary to the letting, apart from a passing break` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the total area of the buildings on it`                                       IS A NUMBER
    `the area that may be built under the plan that applies to it`                IS A NUMBER
    `it is for a use the Minister of Finance fixed, and the fund or a relative of it provides the management services` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is the fund's business inventory`                                         IS A BOOLEAN

-- The kinds of income of a fund in a tax year, for "exceptional income" (הכנסות חריגות), s 64A2(a).
DECLARE `The kind of income of a real-estate investment fund` IS ONE OF
    `income from the sale of business inventory`                                                           -- (1)
    `income from yielding land, land under construction, land for rental housing, or from the sale of building rights in land that was yielding when bought` -- (2)(a)
    `income from securities traded on the stock exchange, from state bonds or from deposits`               -- (2)(b)
    `income that section 7 of the Inflation Adjustments Law treats as business income`                     -- (2)(c)
    `income from the sale of land for rental housing sold before 20 years of letting it as housing, other than a sale to a landlord` -- (3)
    `income from the sale of land that was under construction when bought, sold within four years of its first being used for letting` -- (4)
    `other income`                                                                                         -- (2), the rest

DECLARE `An item of income of a real-estate investment fund` HAS
    `the kind`   IS A `The kind of income of a real-estate investment fund`
    `the amount` IS A NUMBER   -- with land betterment, and without betterment on a sale under s 49KB, 49LG or 49LG1 of the Real Estate Taxation Law

-- Fork Q1. Section 64A2, "exceptional income" (2): "income other than that in (a) to (c) whose total rate exceeds 5% of all the fund's income
-- in the tax year". Is it the whole of that other income that is exceptional once it exceeds 5%, or only the part above 5%?
DECLARE `A reading of the 5% test for other income` IS ONE OF
    `all the other income is exceptional once it is more than 5%`
    `only the part of the other income above 5% is exceptional`
    `declined where the 5% test changes the answer`      -- the default

-- The facts for "land held for a short period" (מקרקעין המוחזקים לתקופה קצרה), s 64A2(a).
DECLARE `A sale of land by a real-estate investment fund` HAS
    `it is land for rental housing`                                                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is land of paragraph (4) of the definition of land for rental housing`              IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day the fund bought it`                                                            IS A DATE
    `the day it became yielding land for rental housing`                                    IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the day it was sold, or sold in an exempt sale`                                        IS A DATE

§§ `Sections 55, 57 and 60A — the kibbutz and its members`

-- How the income of a member of a collective kibbutz or of a renewed kibbutz is assessed.
DECLARE `How the income of a kibbutz member is assessed` IS ONE OF
    `under the sub-chapter on the kibbutz and its members`
    `apart from that sub-chapter, the rates and credit points counted in the kibbutz's assessment and the kibbutz's losses not being counted`

-- A member of a collective kibbutz, for the tax of s 57(a): the figures that decide his tax on an equal share of the kibbutz's income, as if it were his only
-- taxable income. Which credit points and deductions the member's family composition gives (ss 34 to 46A, 47, and Chapter 3 of Part D other than s 66)
-- is for rows IL-01 and IL-02; here they are inputs.
DECLARE `A member of a collective kibbutz` HAS
    `the value of the credit points the member's family is entitled to` IS A NUMBER
    `the deductions allowed under section 47 for the member's family`  IS A NUMBER

§§ `Section 48A of the Real Estate Taxation Law — the tax on betterment`

-- A sale of a right in land, or an action in a land association, with the figures s 48A turns on. The betterment (שבח) is the sale value less the
-- remaining purchase value (s 6(b), s 47); the real betterment is the betterment less the inflationary amount; the chargeable inflationary amount is
-- s 47's. They are computed under ss 39 and 47 of that Law, which this row does not encode (the Law's rates only), and are inputs.
DECLARE `A sale of a right in land, for section 48A` HAS
    `the seller`                                                             IS A `The seller, for section 91`
    `it is an action in a land association`                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the betterment`                                                         IS A NUMBER
    `the real betterment`                                                    IS A NUMBER
    `the chargeable inflationary amount`                                     IS A NUMBER
    `the purchase day`                                                       IS A DATE
    `the sale day`                                                           IS A DATE
    `it is a qualifying residential apartment that section 48A(b2) governs`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the conditions of section 48A(b4) hold`                                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `the consideration was influenced by additional building rights, section 48A(b3)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Director allowed in writing a rate lower than the cap, of`          IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `section 48A(d)(4) excludes the sale`                                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `the seller is a company with business income, or an individual who received the right when a company was wound up` IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `Section 9 of the Real Estate Taxation Law — the purchase tax on a dwelling`

-- The facts of a purchase of a right in a residential apartment that the bands of s 9(c1c), (c1f) turn on.
DECLARE `A purchase of a right in a residential apartment` HAS
    `the day of the sale`                                                                         IS A DATE
    `the value of the right sold`                                                                 IS A NUMBER
    `the buyer is an individual resident in Israel`                                               IS A BOOLEAN   -- (c1c)(2), (4)(b)
    `the apartment is the buyer's only apartment`                                                 IS A BOOLEAN   -- (c1c)(2)(a)
    `the buyer sold the other apartment that was his only one within the period`                  IS A BOOLEAN   -- (c1c)(2)(b)
    `the buyer bought the apartment after a purchase-group apartment was delayed, as (c1c)(2)(b1) says` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (c1c)(2)(b1)
    `the apartment is a replacement apartment as section 49E(a) means`                            IS A BOOLEAN   -- (c1c)(2)(c)

-- Fork P1. Section 9(c1f)(1) taxes a purchase of a dwelling that is not the buyer's only or replacement one at 8% and 10%, for a sale from 28 November 2021 "until
-- 31 December 2024". The consolidation's note after it says the period was extended to 31 December 2026 by an order (Kovetz HaTakanot 5785, 626), which is not deposited.
DECLARE `A reading of the end of the period of section 9(c1f)` IS ONE OF
    `the period ends on 31 December 2024, as the paragraph prints it`
    `the period ends on 31 December 2026, as the consolidation's note on the extension says`
    `declined where the end of the period changes the answer`      -- the default

-- Fork R2. Section 9(c2) rounds an adjusted amount "to the nearest sum that is a multiple of 5 shillings" and does not say where a half goes.
DECLARE `A reading of rounding to a multiple of 5 shillings` IS ONE OF
    `a half goes up`
    `a half goes down`
    `declined where the rounding of a half changes the answer`     -- the default

-- The housing-services index readings that adjust the amounts from 16 January 2028 (s 9(c2)): the index last published before the update day, and the base
-- index published on 15 January 2027.
DECLARE `Index readings for the amounts of section 9(c1c)` HAS
    `the new index, last published before the update day`  IS A NUMBER
    `the base index, published on 15 January 2027`          IS A NUMBER
